---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import { publicLinks, site } from '../config/site';
import { catalog } from '../lib/content';
import { pathFor, formatDate } from '../lib/urls';
const { milestones } = await catalog();
---
<Shell title="About" description={site.bio}>
  <header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">About me</p><h1>Hello, I’m Rinshid.</h1><p class="summary">A CS student, the founder of {site.profile.venture}, and a believer in learning by building.</p></header>
  <article class="prose" id="about">
    <p>My full name is <strong>{site.name}</strong>. I’m from Kerala and study Computer Science &amp; Engineering at TKM College of Engineering. I build practical software and automation, and I want to help other CS students find their footing as technology changes.</p>
    <h2>Helping students adapt to AI</h2>
    <p>I’m interested in how we can learn new tools quickly while still thinking carefully as engineers: understanding the problem, asking better questions, checking outputs, and deciding what is worth building.</p>
    <p>Prompt engineering and context engineering are part of that conversation. So are AI agents, world models, and free and open source software. These are areas I’m exploring and want to explain in accessible ways.</p>
    <h2>Build something. Learn from it.</h2>
    <p>I believe building matters more than just talking about ideas. A working project gives us something concrete to try, question, and improve. My public projects include a desktop break reminder, a lab-code sharing workspace, and an admissions help-desk portal.</p>
    <p>This notebook connects those projects with their technical decisions and limitations. I want to share useful explanations through writing and speaking, in English and Malayalam, as I continue learning.</p>
    <h2>Time and attention matter too</h2>
    <p>Keeping up with technology is only one part of the challenge. I also care about productivity, personal development, and how we protect our attention in a world of social-media feeds and constant distractions.</p>
    <p>I want to explore habits that help us make time for learning and building—and be thoughtful about how we spend the rest of our day.</p>
    <h2 id="experience">Work &amp; experience</h2>
    <dl class="experience-list">
      <div><dt>{site.profile.venture} · {site.profile.role}</dt><dd>I’m the founder of {site.profile.venture}. Practical software and automation are part of my work.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>{site.profile.previousWork.organization} · Automation work</dt><dd><span class="meta">{site.profile.previousWork.period} · Past work</span>{site.profile.previousWork.contribution} This work ended in August 2026.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <h2 id="skills">Tools, in context</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Automation:</strong> n8n workflows and AWS in my past work for Azmora.</li>
      <li><strong>Web applications:</strong> React, TypeScript, Supabase, and PostgreSQL in student-facing projects; TanStack Start in the KEAM portal.</li>
      <li><strong>Desktop utilities:</strong> Tauri and Rust alongside React for BlinkBreak.</li>
      <li><strong>Working in public:</strong> Git and GitHub for source, release notes, and project discussions.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="education">Education</h2><p>{site.profile.education}. Expected graduation: {site.profile.graduation}.</p>
  </article>
  {milestones.length > 0 && <section class="section"><h2>Along the way</h2><ol class="timeline">{milestones.map((entry) => <li><p class="meta">{formatDate(entry.data.date)} · {entry.data.role}</p><h3>{entry.data.title}</h3><p>{entry.data.summary}</p><a href={entry.data.source}>Source ↗</a></li>)}</ol></section>}
  <section class="section"><h2>Let’s compare notes</h2><p class="section-intro">Student questions, project feedback, and useful collaborations are welcome.</p><div class="link-row">{publicLinks.filter((link) => link.featured).map((link) => <a href={link.url}>{link.platform} ↗</a>)}<a href={pathFor('/contact/')}>Get in touch →</a></div></section>
</Shell>
